# Rust build output — regenerable, large, never committed.
/target/

# Cargo.lock is NOT committed for this lib-only workspace.
# Standard Rust library practice: applications commit Cargo.lock for
# reproducible builds; libraries omit it so downstream resolvers are not
# pinned by the library author. This workspace ships no binaries, so the
# lockfile would only add merge noise. (If a binary/example target or a
# crates.io-published app is added later, revisit: commit Cargo.lock then.)
Cargo.lock

# Compiler / editor backups.
**/*.rs.bk

# IDE directories — contributors use whatever editor they like; none of
# these belong in version control.
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS noise (Windows/macOS file-manager artifacts).
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
